From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Priestley <Voicedrew11@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 00:28:03 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 41/41] vu1: run lifted microprogram segments (PS2X_VU1_LIFT)

A lifted segment is a C++ translation of one VU1 microcode segment with
a static, cycle-exact schedule, registered by (FNV-1a hash of the micro
memory, start pc). With PS2X_VU1_LIFT=1, VU1Interpreter::run calls a
registered segment instead of interpreting when the pipelines are idle
and leaves the state the interpreter would: registers, flags, Q/P, data
memory, cycle count and PATH1 output (the transfer advances in step with
the segment's stores). It runs to the end of the segment; the cycle
budget only bounds the interpreter's time slice.

runtime/ps2_vu1_lift.h holds the helpers the generated code uses (FMAC
with exact flag classification, FDIV, ESADD, CLIP, conversions, stores
and XGKICK). Lifted sources in src/vu1lift/ are compiled into the runner
(not part of this repository; they are generated per game).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
